                <pb facs="pe_d14-1" n="1" xml:id="pe_d14-1"/>

                <head>PE–14. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Public Law 532, Both Congress, approved July 18, 1958, authorized the transfer of
                    naval vessels to friendly foreign countries (72 State 376). In telegram 68 to
                    Lima, August 13, the Department of State instructed <pb facs="1137" n="1049"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg1049"/> the Embassy to offer two destroyers to Peru
                    for $7 million rehabilitation costs. (723.5–MSP/8–1358) Documentation concerning
                    the ensuing negotiations for transfer of naval vessels is in files 723.5–MSP,
                    723.56, 723.5621, and 723.5622. By an exchange of notes at Lima on February 12
                    and 26, 1960, the two Governments agreed to a five-year loan of three United
                    States naval vessels (one destroyer and two frigates) to Peru. For the text of
                    the agreement, see II UST (pt. 2) 2254. In an exchange of notes at Washington,
                    December 27 and 28, 1960, the two Governments agreed to a five-year loan of a
                    destroyer to Peru with the cost of rehabilitation and equipment charged to Peru.
                    For the text of this agreement, see 12 UST 364.</p>
